GAL22V10
TILEGLZ2

BCLK  BLATCH RLATCH TW  BFIRST TDATA LDATA BDATA NC   NC    NC   GND
NC    Q0     Q1     Q2  Q3     BW    TCLK  LCLK  LATCH HX   DS   VCC

; Corrected variant of hardware/gal/tile_glue.pld: recovers TRUE tri-state T_clk
; (rev-A electrical behaviour) inside the same 10-macrocell budget.
; Trade: the NPL macrocell output is dropped; the two '165 ~PL pins are driven by
; an external 74LVC1G04 fed from the LATCH pin (tile = GAL + 2x'165 + 1G04 = 4 ICs).
;
; The 22V10 gives each macrocell ONE output-enable product term. T_clk's enable is
; an OR (/TW + /BFIRST), not a product -> the committed design drove T_clk low
; instead. Here a helper macrocell HX = /TW + /BFIRST (a sum is fine for a data
; equation) is fed back as the single-literal product term TCLK.E.

; --- bit counter (unchanged) ---
Q0.R  = /Q0
Q1.R  = Q1 * /Q0 + /Q1 * Q0
Q2.R  = Q2 * /Q1 + Q2 * /Q0 + /Q2 * Q1 * Q0
Q3.R  = Q3 * /Q2 + Q3 * /Q1 + Q3 * /Q0 + /Q3 * Q2 * Q1 * Q0
Q0.E  = GND
Q1.E  = GND
Q2.E  = GND
Q3.E  = GND

; --- column-end flag (unchanged) ---
BW.R  = BW + BDATA * Q0 * Q1 * Q2 * Q3

; --- helper: "top clock selected" as one feedback literal ---
HX.T  = /TW + /BFIRST
HX.E  = GND

; --- clocks: BOTH truly tri-stated when unselected, as U101/U107 in rev A ---
TCLK.T = BCLK
TCLK.E = HX
LCLK.T = BCLK
LCLK.E = TW * BFIRST

; --- latch merge --- (the '165 ~PL now comes from an external 1G04 on LATCH)
LATCH = BLATCH + RLATCH

; --- serial input (unchanged) ---
DS    = TW * BFIRST * LDATA + /TW * TDATA + /BFIRST * TDATA

AR    = LATCH
SP    = GND

DESCRIPTION

Isomorphic keyboard tile, rev-A/B glue in one ATF22LV10C, variant with true-Z T_clk.
Behavioural equivalence to rev A (including the Z) is checked in ../equivalence/.
Macrocells: Q0..Q3, BW, TCLK, LCLK, LATCH, HX, DS = 10 of 10; no NPL pin.
